{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1555087-humanity-adaptability-elseworlds","id":1555087,"title":"Humanity, adaptability, elseworlds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-11-04T19:26:32-08:00","id":1555087,"title":"Humanity, adaptability, elseworlds","content":"Do we have any information on could humans survive in other worlds and realms, wether they got themselves there or some mages decided to experiment?<br /> <br /> Long story short, could humans survive and in what way in many realms that are connected to Earth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T00:20:12-08:00","id":1555098,"title":"","content":"Yes, with caveats.<br /> <br /> Long story short, any place a Mage can stay, a human can, too. Which in the barest sense means any realm, none of them is inherently hostile to human life. That said, survival may pose a challenge just as it would any dangerous environment on Earth, on top of the challenge of getting them there (which isn't terribly hard for most, but is for some).<br /> <br /> The main problems are dangerous local inhabitants and, depending on the place, getting water and food (air isn't usually a problem).<br /> <br /> <b>Abyss</b> - Anything can happen, anyone is unlikely to survive long. Leaving a human here is asking for shit to happen, just as leaving anything here, including Mages.<br /> <br /> <b>Astral</b> - Usually death in it only means being released in the waking world again, although there may be exceptions. It's unclear if dream-stuff can sustain humans physically transported here, but otherwise they're fine. This is probably the safest place for a human, and Beasts actually bring them physically with some frequency.<br /> <br /> <b>Duat</b> - Nothing dies for real in this realm, although bringing anyone here is quite a challenge to begin with. Even then, it happens. That said, this place will cause a lot of suffering and probably trigger a lot of Breaking Points, so it isn't really safer than the Astral. It's unclear what happens when a non-Mummy completes the journey through Duat, if they'll be judged by the Judges and what they'll do to a living mortal depending on their verdict.<br /> <br /> <b>Hedge</b> - Humans can live here as normal and eat and drink local edibles. Those edibles may or may not have weird effects, that may or may not render them unsafe. The environment is dangerous in many ways, the locals are dangerous in many ways, and simply staying here for long may cause weird shit to anything that isn't an inhabitant <i>yet</i>. IIRC now there are even rules for humans living here to become a particular kind of Goblin, but I didn't read 2nd Edition yet.<br /> <br /> <b>Neter-Khertet</b> - This particular manifestation of Death Twilight has added denizens that are very dangerous to humans, especially the Amkhata, and a storm that mostly hides things. Also there are visible passages to both the Underworld and Duat, that a human may then try to use if they're here. It is otherwise like any other Twilight, which means you have to bring food and water from elsewhere.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow</b> - It may be that a human left for years in the Shadow start to become something else, but in principle nothing exceptional happens. I'm almost sure humans can survive on local &quot;food&quot;, but getting it is tricky as everything is a spirit or at least spirit-stuff that can become a spirit eventually. Surviving the local &quot;fauna&quot; in general is hard.<br /> <br /> <b>Underworld</b> - Definitely devoid of food, although it has water. Drinking from the Rivers is not advisable as they may have many weird effects, but rarely they'll be life-threatening if you're left with no choice. They may also be made of things like blood, pus, metal chains, whatever, but they're all actually drinkable (they still taste as they look). The water trickling down through the upper caves is usually safer, but the best option for a living being is still to bring water and food. Food may get stale a little faster here, but not terribly so, and it won't actually rot AFAIK. If you manage to cross the rivers, which is doable if not cheap, the Dead Dominions may be infinitely varied, so it isn't impossible to find one where you have food fit for humans. I wouldn't count on it, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T01:55:18-08:00","id":1555103,"title":"","content":"I think it was <i>Deviant's Clade Companion</i> that describes how <b>Inferno</b> is survivable for living humans trapped there. I don't remember what it said about hell's dangerous environments, but food is interesting there. There are delicious feasts to be found there, but they provide no nourishment. You can also find disgusting muck that's difficult to force down without gagging. It's the only thing that can keep your body going.<br /> <br /> You can find food in the <b>Shadow</b> as well, but what counts as food can be surprising. Chasing down something &quot;living&quot; is your best bet. Processed foods, though... <i>Book of Spirits</i> from 1st edition described how you can empty a bag of chips, only to vomit afterwards and see your bile reconstitute into a pristine unopened bag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T03:08:18-08:00","id":1555106,"title":"","content":"What level of survival do you mean? Like, there are lots of places where you can probably scavenge for the bare essentials of life for at least a while. Or do you mean, like building a colony in another realm?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T06:52:43-08:00","id":1555117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1555087-humanity-adaptability-elseworlds?p=1555098#post1555098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Abyss</b> - Anything can happen, anyone is unlikely to survive long. Leaving a human here is asking for shit to happen, just as leaving anything here, including Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Caveat here that there is a significant distinction between &quot;the Abyss&quot; and &quot;Abyssal worlds/Greater Abyssal beings,&quot; with the latter having consistent, if nearly incomprehensible, laws of their own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Hedge</b> - Humans can live here as normal and eat and drink local edibles. Those edibles may or may not have weird effects, that may or may not render them unsafe. The environment is dangerous in many ways, the locals are dangerous in many ways, and simply staying here for long may cause weird shit to anything that isn't an inhabitant <i>yet</i>. IIRC now there are even rules for humans living here to become a particular kind of Goblin, but I didn't read 2nd Edition yet. </div> </div> </div>Goblin Debt from using Goblin Contracts or making deals with hobgoblins (or more particular methods, like mages releasing Paradoxes in the Hedge) turns anyone who accumulates enough of it into a Hedge Denizen, with those who lose Touchstones and some of their Integrity-equivalent becoming Goblin Queens; <i>The Hedge</i> goes into greater detail on what life as a hobgoblin is like, as well as adding means of finding normal nourishing food and drink to the options available through Hedgespinning (it's of the sort that any fae creature can do, in contrast to the more involved and dramatic environmental shifts that are the province of changelings, Huntsmen, and True Fae).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Underworld</b> - Definitely devoid of food, although it has water. Drinking from the Rivers is not advisable as they may have many weird effects, but rarely they'll be life-threatening if you're left with no choice. They may also be made of things like blood, pus, metal chains, whatever, but they're all actually drinkable (they still taste as they look). The water trickling down through the upper caves is usually safer, but the best option for a living being is still to bring water and food. Food may get stale a little faster here, but not terribly so, and it won't actually rot AFAIK. If you manage to cross the rivers, which is doable if not cheap, the Dead Dominions may be infinitely varied, so it isn't impossible to find one where you have food fit for humans. I wouldn't count on it, though. </div> </div> </div>It is a consistently described element of the Underworld that anything edible you find there will not sustain the living \u2014 stuff you bring yourself is likely fair game, but ofrendas and the like are food for ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-05-2025, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T15:10:52-08:00","id":1555137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1555087-humanity-adaptability-elseworlds?p=1555106#post1555106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What level of survival do you mean? Like, there are lots of places where you can probably scavenge for the bare essentials of life for at least a while. Or do you mean, like building a colony in another realm?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, more along the line of a colony in another realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T15:16:47-08:00","id":1555138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1555087-humanity-adaptability-elseworlds?p=1555103#post1555103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it was <i>Deviant's Clade Companion</i> that describes how <b>Inferno</b> is survivable</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't know there was a book that actually described Inferno, since the book that introduced it basically made it a non-place. Which other books describe it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1555087-humanity-adaptability-elseworlds?p=1555117#post1555117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Caveat here that there is a significant distinction between &quot;the Abyss&quot; and &quot;Abyssal worlds/Greater Abyssal beings,&quot; with the latter having consistent, if nearly incomprehensible, laws of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know enough of Mage yet to have the details, so I was keeping to the simpler side of things.<br /> <br /> Theoretically everything is possible, so nothing bad happening is also possible. But that's extremely unlikely, while the most probable results of leaving a human there for months is that they'll perish and the body will be effectively irretrievable, making the details all but irrelevant. Suffice to know it was horrible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1555087-humanity-adaptability-elseworlds?p=1555117#post1555117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Goblin Debt from using Goblin Contracts or making deals with hobgoblins (or more particular methods, like mages releasing Paradoxes in the Hedge) turns anyone who accumulates enough of it into a Hedge Denizen</div> </div> </div> </div>At least that means <i>not </i>becoming a Hedge Denizen is relatively easy if you have the means to survive on your own, which can be mundane (or almost mundane). A Mage that leaves the human with enough resources can reasonably expect the human to still be human in the future.<br /> <br /> Can you find edible things in the Hedge <i>without</i> Hedgespinning?<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1555087-humanity-adaptability-elseworlds?p=1555117#post1555117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a consistently described element of the Underworld that anything edible you find there will not sustain the living \u2014 stuff you bring yourself is likely fair game, but ofrendas and the like are food for ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but it's also an element of the Underworld that the Dominions exist in infinite potential variety (even if they're not actually infinite in number at any given time), so a Dominion that breaks that rule wouldn't be impossible. Extremely unlikely, certainly, but not impossible. Hades' pomegranate seeds come to mind.<br /> <br /> This is more of a side note, anyway, a thought exercise. An ST that wants such Dominion would be running a very specific sort of game anyway, on most games a normal human won't travel that far into the caves even if thrown in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Overall living in the Underworld is feasible, but requires access to the outside for food. It could even be access to another Realm like the Shadow or the Astral, as both have access points to the Underworld and possibly have edible resources.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T15:23:30-08:00","id":1555139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rosencroft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1555087-humanity-adaptability-elseworlds?p=1555137#post1555137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, more along the line of a colony in another realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>In most of them, yes.<br /> <br /> Some will require outside sources of food, and most will require fortifications and weapons. but only the Abyss is inherently hostile and none other will simply vanish with your resources with no warning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T18:27:21-08:00","id":1555147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1555087-humanity-adaptability-elseworlds?p=1555138#post1555138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't know there was a book that actually described Inferno, since the book that introduced it basically made it a non-place. Which other books describe it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Clades Companion for Deviant has a functional stealth-update for the Inferno, detailing Malapraxes and giving the working unified name of &quot;devils&quot; for the demons of the Inferno. It's still pretty difficult to escape an open Hellmouth if you get too close and looking into one shows you personalized horrors that inflict conditions from the &quot;dramatically fail a breaking point roll&quot; list.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Theoretically everything is possible, so nothing bad happening is also possible. But that's extremely unlikely, while the most probable results of leaving a human there for months is that they'll perish and the body will be effectively irretrievable, making the details all but irrelevant. Suffice to know it was horrible. </div> </div> </div>I mention this mainly because, while getting tossed into the Abyss is typically a one-way trip, world-beings of the sort that make beachheads into ordered reality have denizens close enough to human to justify &quot;a doppleganger of the spellcaster emerges&quot; as an example Manifestation Paradox in Mage 1e (and one of the sample characters from 2e discusses in the fiction anthology his memories of another life in a particular Abyssal world), so in cases where the goal is survival rather than escape the distinction is significant \u2014 the rules can change from moment to moment in the wider Abyss, but you can learn to live in the Annunaki.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At least that means <i>not </i>becoming a Hedge Denizen is relatively easy if you have the means to survive on your own, which can be mundane (or almost mundane). A Mage that leaves the human with enough resources can reasonably expect the human to still be human in the future.<br /> <br /> Can you find edible things in the Hedge <i>without</i> Hedgespinning? </div> </div> </div>No, but with luck or the right approach one could steer the Hedge's natural process of spinning itself toward providing normal food if relying on the aid of hobgoblins doesn't serve, and becoming a hobgoblin is itself a reversible process largely boiling down to working off some of the Debt to your creditor and then gaining or losing Integrity-equivalent. (Given that goblin fruits do not sustain non-fae, it is debatably prudent to take a stint as a hobgoblin for survivability so you can work towards finding a way out, but that is admittedly How They Get You.)<br /> <br /> There's also a Fate 2 + Mind 2 spell called Malleable Thorns that lets a mage state a goal for the Hedge to spin itself to somehow fulfill using a number of Hedgespinning successes equal to the spell's Potency; food that isn't high-quality or specific takes four successes, whereas more particular fare takes six successes and would require a Reach for Malleable Thorns to be able to produce, and if the way that food is provided is in the form of a pre-existing larder there is a distinct possibility some predator or other opportunist is hanging around to take advantage of the creatures it attracts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-06T00:30:40-08:00","id":1555156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rosencroft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1555087-humanity-adaptability-elseworlds#post1555087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we have any information on could humans survive in other worlds and realms, wether they got themselves there or some mages decided to experiment?<br /> <br /> Long story short, could humans survive and in what way in many realms that are connected to Earth?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wanted to add something. Not specific to your question, I think the responses have been great. I'd really recommend the Book of Spirits. It really focuses on what the Shadow is like for a mere mortal, down to strange diseases they might pick up there.<br /> <br /> But in Werewolf's Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon, a new group was introduced called RD-13. They're a group who have discovered the science and technology needed to break through to other worlds. And so far they've mapped three, one is the Shadow, another the Underworld, and the third world &quot;is hissing steam, crackling electricity, and grinding cogs. Its geometry collapses upon itself like drawings of illogical shapes, with machines of infinite size impossibly stacked and folded into tiny singularities.&quot; They test dangerously and &quot;volunteers&quot; often come down with mutations, but they're still out there, humans finding new worlds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-06T03:58:39-08:00","id":1555158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rosencroft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1555087-humanity-adaptability-elseworlds?p=1555137#post1555137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, more along the line of a colony in another realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>As others have said, it's possible in quite a few different ones, and there are examples in the books, but it basically never works long-term. The only real exception is the Astral, but that's not really a place you live. I gather that this is more or less a design specification; Mage: The Ascension had a bunch of effectively off-world colonies which it was felt by designers to be detrimental to the setting. So Mage: The Awakening just avoids it from the issue from the start.<br /> <br /> The big example that comes to mind is the 'Adytum of the Mystery' from <i>Mysterium</i>. Basically mages built a city in the Shadow. Apparently, it was very impressive, but last time anyone visited it was totally empty of people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-06T11:20:03-08:00","id":1555166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1555087-humanity-adaptability-elseworlds?p=1555138#post1555138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't know there was a book that actually described Inferno, since the book that introduced it basically made it a non-place. Which other books describe it?</div> </div> </div> </div>As Satchel implied, only <i>Inferno</i> and <i>Clades Companion</i> go into it in any depth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-06T15:24:42-08:00","id":1555185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1555087-humanity-adaptability-elseworlds?p=1555147#post1555147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Clades Companion for Deviant has a functional stealth-update for the Inferno, detailing Malapraxes and giving the working unified name of &quot;devils&quot; for the demons of the Inferno. It's still pretty difficult to escape an open Hellmouth if you get too close and looking into one shows you personalized horrors that inflict conditions from the &quot;dramatically fail a breaking point roll&quot; list.<br /> <br /> I mention this mainly because, while getting tossed into the Abyss is typically a one-way trip, world-beings of the sort that make beachheads into ordered reality have denizens close enough to human to justify &quot;a doppleganger of the spellcaster emerges&quot; as an example Manifestation Paradox in Mage 1e (and one of the sample characters from 2e discusses in the fiction anthology his memories of another life in a particular Abyssal world), so in cases where the goal is survival rather than escape the distinction is significant \u2014 the rules can change from moment to moment in the wider Abyss, but you can learn to live in the Annunaki.<br /> <br /> No, but with luck or the right approach one could steer the Hedge's natural process of spinning itself toward providing normal food if relying on the aid of hobgoblins doesn't serve, and becoming a hobgoblin is itself a reversible process largely boiling down to working off some of the Debt to your creditor and then gaining or losing Integrity-equivalent. (Given that goblin fruits do not sustain non-fae, it is debatably prudent to take a stint as a hobgoblin for survivability so you can work towards finding a way out, but that is admittedly How They Get You.)<br /> <br /> There's also a Fate 2 + Mind 2 spell called Malleable Thorns that lets a mage state a goal for the Hedge to spin itself to somehow fulfill using a number of Hedgespinning successes equal to the spell's Potency; food that isn't high-quality or specific takes four successes, whereas more particular fare takes six successes and would require a Reach for Malleable Thorns to be able to produce, and if the way that food is provided is in the form of a pre-existing larder there is a distinct possibility some predator or other opportunist is hanging around to take advantage of the creatures it attracts.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, from here we take:<br /> <br /> 1- A well prepared trip to the <b>Abyss</b> may deliver you somewhere survivable and stable enough. Would it be safe long term enough for a human colony? Maybe;<br /> <br /> 2- You can make a colony in the <b>Hedge</b>. Providing food and water is a challenge, but with enough experts with the right training, or a single Mage with the right Arcanoi/Rote, it can be done locally;<br /> <br /> 3- With that, you can make a colony in any and every Realm but Inferno, given you have the right tools. Granted, you don't really need exceptional tools, although you'll need heavy firepower most of the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1555087-humanity-adaptability-elseworlds?p=1555158#post1555158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but it basically never works long-term.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not strictly true.<br /> <br /> We don't have <i><b>examples</b></i> of long duration colonies in other realms, but we don't have examples of a lot of things because the setting is pretty open-ended. It not only is theoretically possible, there may exist something already in any given chronicle without going against canon.<br /> <br /> In fact, <i><b>Deviant</b></i> goes as far as to say that some Conspiracies can have otherworldly bases, without specifying in which realm.<br /> <br /> Sure, any colony would require a lot of preparation and work, and you have no guarantees in the long run. It would take a lot of resources, or a lot of extremely resourceful people, or both.<br /> <br /> But at least in theory it is doable, and all otherworlds have safer regions where you can try.<br /> <br /> Just be sure to be ready for fighting the inhabitants, and it won't be easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-06T16:55:06-08:00","id":1555188,"title":"","content":"Personally, I find some of the premise of Annunaki as bubbles of coherence within the Abyss to kind of shift it away from what I regard as some of the more intriguing prospects of that plane.<br /> <br /> I choose to reconcile this in terms of the Annunaki having coherence only along certain subjective frames of reference. Like, imagine you saw the Nemesis Continuum from afar. &quot;Good&quot;, you think; &quot;a place to stand where I don't have to worry that any given section of my body might randomly change shape or become subjected to different laws of physics or gain independent sapience or have its colours become different parts of a spectrum that cause them to mix and annihilate one another or-&quot;.<br /> <br /> You approach the Nemesis Continuum and step confidently into its boundaries. Only to discover that, what looked coherent from afar, was actually a trick of perspective; all of its different parts are at separate distances from one another, such that it all looks singular and connected when viewed from the right angle, but is spread out from right up close, with all the undifferentiated Abyss in between. It is the nature of the slumbering gods of the Abyss that they can be fully themselves even when interspersed like this, but that is not a reality shared by most hypothetical visitors.<br /> <br /> You smack your forehead in frustration, and instantly shatter from a sudden new fragility, the shards of you fluttering away as butterflies on the breeze before passing through a shaft of sunlight that refracts them into bubbles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-06T17:43:16-08:00","id":1555189,"title":"","content":"Thank you for all answers, and if I may, can I ask this?<br /> What are the odds of humanity surviving/existing in a Lower Depth realm that lacks Death ( nothing stays dead ) compared to a crafted pocket realm a size of a small planet?<br /> Provided, there is water and local &quot;flora&quot; and &quot;fauna&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-06T17:49:31-08:00","id":1555190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1555087-humanity-adaptability-elseworlds?p=1555188#post1555188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I find some of the premise of Annunaki as bubbles of coherence within the Abyss to kind of shift it away from what I regard as some of the more intriguing prospects of that plane.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, in fact, objectively the case, because, to use the most direct example, that's how Gulmoth work. Abyssal beings as discrete phenomena are not ruinous to reality because of some intrinsic protean quality; they are ruinous to reality because the principles they work on are antithetical to the portion of reality that needs to not be impossible in order to function Anumerous does not need to be able to pull a heretofore unforeseen aspect of his powers out of his back pocket to continue to be an anti-symbol of Numbers Gone Wrong that paves the way for the unmaking of ordered reality. The Third of Two is not going to become the Gears of Chaos, because it is the Third of Two and nothing else. The Dur-Abzu exist to negate the symbolism of their Supernal counterparts and they aren't going to change the thrust of that counter-symbolism purely for the sake of embodying the destruction of reason, hope, and being in a broader sense.<br /> <br /> Greater Abyssal Beings are universes unto themselves; not all of them are hospitable to Phenomenal humanity, but the ones that are are so in a consistent fashion, and that does not stop them from destroying the poor fool who pokes around the wrong part of their awful systems any more than the Earth is unable to consume an amateur volcanologist.<br /> <br /> None of this detracts from the Void itself being the chaotic boundary between the Ideal and the Real \u2014 &quot;sufficiently powerful beings can create self-contained worlds where things are more predictable, but all of them ultimately degrade reality&quot; is straight from Imperial Mysteries, and it echoes similar circumstances in Arcadia and the Underworld re: bubbles of more ordered (albeit strange) existence amid a shifting bed of chaos far from material reality. Yes, it might all collapse some day because its god got bored, but that's still <i>the end of a world</i>, not business as usual within its context.<br /> <br /> I've mulled over the Abyss's presentation in the books as specifically more than just shapeless cosmic horror for long enough to recognize that &quot;anti-symbol&quot; isn't a meaningless abstract concept when placed next to the aggregate trends of Abyssal beings and antinomian magic. You have to be able to use the tools the game gives you in a more robust sense than implying a Rank 9 pure sodium hypercube the size of the Sun is minutes away from popping into existence from pure possibility-space if the intention of a game is to engage with the Abyss as a narrative device with variety and nuance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-06T18:02:49-08:00","id":1555191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rosencroft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1555087-humanity-adaptability-elseworlds?p=1555189#post1555189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the odds of humanity surviving/existing in a Lower Depth realm that lacks Death ( nothing stays dead ) compared to a crafted pocket realm a size of a small planet?<br /> Provided, there is water and local &quot;flora&quot; and &quot;fauna&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Entry to the Lower Depths is typically a one-way trip and a realm lacking Death is one where nothing <i>dies</i> \u2014 &quot;choked with endless knots of imperishable flesh and plant matter&quot; is how that specific example is described in the corebook, to say nothing of the sort of weird tumorous amoebas that might subsist on minerals and ambient gases.<br /> <br /> The pocket realm is dramatically more survivable if you're including the things humans need to survive, because it is a place that is made for humans to be able to survive. The Depth is going to need an environmental suit at best, and in the grand scheme of things is more likely to be instantly fatal or indistinguishable from a seafloor lab or an isolated deep-space station.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-06T18:38:36-08:00","id":1555194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rosencroft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1555087-humanity-adaptability-elseworlds?p=1555189#post1555189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for all answers, and if I may, can I ask this?<br /> What are the odds of humanity surviving/existing in a Lower Depth realm that lacks Death ( nothing stays dead ) compared to a crafted pocket realm a size of a small planet?<br /> Provided, there is water and local &quot;flora&quot; and &quot;fauna&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Lower Depths realms are governed by Death Gods, and it isn't entirely clear if they have a hand in their creation, but if not they're entirely natural.<br /> <br /> That means if the ST wants such a place to exist, it exists. If they don't, it doesn't. And on top of that they'll have their Laws.<br /> <br /> Human colonizers don't have any means to either create, promote or locate such places. And Dead Dominions are finite in number, so just because something is possible it doesn't mean it exists.<br /> <br /> So... the odds of surviving there depends entirely on the specific realm, but the odds of such a place existing to begin with are extremely low, the odds of it being without exceptional danger that may impede a large colony entirely are also extremely low, and the odds of finding it are also quite low. The journey will also be dangerous. And then you have to ponder your relationship to local gods.<br /> <br /> And in every case it all depends on the denizens of the area. The truth of the matter is that, for one reason or another, truly hostile environments are actually rarer in the otherworlds than on Earth. Extreme weather, dryness, exposure to sun or wind, all those are at most as common than on Earth, frequently rarer or more manageable in some way. What really makes them dangerous are the denizens, and those can usually get pretty strong.<br /> <br /> Whenever you go, you can expect Ephemeral Entities of Rank 1 or 2 to be around regularly and be frequently hostile, and Entities of greater rank are close enough to take notice of you sooner or later, all the way up to Rank 5 at least, or the equivalent in power in non-Ephemeral entities. In a Dead Dominion you'll have to deal with an average at least 1 Rank higher (more the deeper it is), which is a problem, but they're also the most human-like in the otherworlds, so you can at least try to talk with many of them.<br /> <br /> It all depends, then, on whatever &quot;lives&quot; in the Dominion. Living humans have a lot to offer that they may want to take, or may want to negotiate so it isn't eliminated. Depending on many things the colony may be either quickly under siege, have a harsh but manageable life, to even raised as cattle or actively patronized by local powers. Learning about the local denizens and how to deal with them is an important thing here.<br /> <br /> Now, all that is before adding the &quot;lacks Death&quot; part. That's as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> said, it will be a very weird environment and probably quite dangerous and toxic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-06T19:21:10-08:00","id":1555195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1555087-humanity-adaptability-elseworlds?p=1555194#post1555194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lower Depths realms are governed by Death Gods, and it isn't entirely clear if they have a hand in their creation, but if not they're entirely natural.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chiming in because this looks like a mixup I've seen before: The Lower Depths are extremely inhospitable portions of thin reality that are generally missing one or more things necessary for life, as metaphysically divorced from the rest of the Phenomenal World as the Phenomenal is from the Supernal \u2014 they're the Hell to the Supernal's Heaven, to the point where the Inferno was originally what &quot;the Lower Depths&quot; referred to before some circles needed to be squared re: different books describing them different ways, and the other semi-defined parts of the cosmology that share the label now are Duat from Mummy and the place powerful Strix can use the Dark Places Manifestation to open a gateway to in Vampire.<br /> <br /> &quot;Off the map and wants to eat us&quot; is the irreverent shorthand that was used at one point to describe Lower Depths on the forums, and the Alexandrian Dark Era mentions them in its cosmology primer with the distinctive phrasing of &quot;Not all of them are evil, but none of them are good.&quot; What little we know of most of them doesn't really involve capital-L Laws.<br /> <br /> Dead Dominions are part of the Lower <i>Mysteries</i>, the part of the Underworld past the Rivers that separate them from the <i>Autochthonous </i>Depths on the top layer of that world (not counting ghostly Twilight/Neter-Khertet); the chthonians that can be found in the Rivers and Ocean of the Underworld may have some connection to the Lower Depths, but they inhabit a part of the cosmology that isn't directly antithetical to life and can be consistently returned from by anyone with the ability to open its doors with freely-used magical powers (as opposed to ritual Keys).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-07T02:17:41-08:00","id":1555199,"title":"","content":"Given that it's implied to be a kind of anti-Supernal World, I'd tend to think the Abyss works very similar, ie. actually going there leads to your erasure from reality unless you're an Archmaster*. I don't think we ever get the Abyss itself described, it always seems to be mediated via the Fallen World in some manner.<br /> <br /> *or being initiated by a ziggurat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rosencroft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1555087-humanity-adaptability-elseworlds?p=1555189#post1555189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the odds of humanity surviving/existing in a Lower Depth realm that lacks Death ( nothing stays dead ) compared to a crafted pocket realm a size of a small planet? Provided, there is water and local &quot;flora&quot; and &quot;fauna&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's your fiction, so whatever you want. I am curious how you're going to eat things that can't die, but that's presumably the kind of weirdness you're looking for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T05:58:10-08:00","id":1555235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1555087-humanity-adaptability-elseworlds?p=1555199#post1555199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that it's implied to be a kind of anti-Supernal World, I'd tend to think the Abyss works very similar, ie. actually going there leads to your erasure from reality unless you're an Archmaster*. I don't think we ever get the Abyss itself described, it always seems to be mediated via the Fallen World in some manner.<br /> <br /> *or being initiated by a ziggurat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is generally the case if you manage to chuck something straight into the Abyss, but that's rarely the case* since actual portals to the Abyss are generally connect to Annunaki, that form versions of &quot;reality&quot; which <i>could</i> be a lot more hospitable than the pure chaotic energies of unordered Abyss.<br /> <br /> *unless you count the Ocean Oroboros which is technically &quot;just&quot; the Astral representation of the Abyss","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}